            "id": "0002-section-breadcrumb"
          },
          {
            "type": "section",
            "value": {
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "<h2>Overview</h2><p>OpenStax Text renders exactly like the plain <b>Text</b> block — it proxies the same rich-text renderer, and takes the same single rich-text field, with no extra config. What it adds is the openstax-cms editor styles.</p><p>It ships in <code>@openstax/flex-page-os-blocks</code> and is registered under its own block type, <code>os_text</code>, alongside the generic <code>text</code> block — so a page can use either. The editor styles are scoped to this block, so a plain <b>Text</b> block renders the same markup without them.</p>",
                  "id": "0003-text-overview"
                }
              ],
              "config": [
                {
                  "type": "padding_bottom",
                  "value": 1,
                  "id": "0003-cfg-pad"
                }
              ]
            },
            "id": "0003-section-overview"
          },
          {
            "type": "section",
            "value": {
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "value": "<h2>Editor styles</h2><p>These are openstax-cms editor classes the content team applies to runs of text in the rich-text editor — they're part of the content, not block config. The <code>eyebrow</code> class renders as a small uppercase label, typically above a heading, and <code>text-blue</code>, <code>text-green</code>, <code>text-orange</code>, <code>text-gray</code>, and <code>text-white</code> apply the OpenStax brand colors to any run of text. For example:</p>",
                  "id": "0004-text-editor-styles"
                },
                {
                  "type": "os_text",
                  "value": "<p class=\"eyebrow\">Free + Openly Licensed</p><h3>College Physics</h3><p>OpenStax brand colors on inline runs: <span class=\"text-blue\">blue</span>, <span class=\"text-green\">green</span>, <span class=\"text-orange\">orange</span>, and <span class=\"text-gray\">gray</span>.</p>",
                  "id": "0004-os-text-example"
                }
              ],
              "config": [
                {
                  "type": "padding_bottom",
                  "value": 1,
                  "id": "0004-cfg-pad"
                }
              ]
            },
            "id": "0004-section-editor-styles"
          }
        ]
      }
